title ALES144 — Lotus's stereo_schmitt: the Schmitt trigger carried into stereo, the first STATE-CARRYING comparator in stereo, one shared band and two independent rails
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Fresh recur turn. Last landed the stereo dead-zone family whole (ALES141 hard center clip · ALES142 soft · ALES143 infinite clip), all MEMORYLESS comparators. Crux-first, the natural next member of the comparator class is ALES92's Schmitt trigger — the first STATE-CARRYING member, harder because it carries a bit (which rail am I on), which is exactly what makes the stereo lift genuinely new rather than a fourth copy of the same odd-map shape.
think ALES92's schmitt flips high on a rise past t_high, low on a fall past t_low, holds between — the band [t_low, t_high] a dead zone the noise cannot rattle. Carried into stereo it carries ONE BIT PER CHANNEL: each channel remembers its own rail, both opened from the shared low-rail convention, so the two rails advance INDEPENDENTLY. The distinctive law: an identical-channel master stays identical (rails track together), yet an out-of-phase master is NOT held out of phase — the honest PARTING from the memoryless family, whose odd maps held the antisymmetry. The from-silence convention opens both channels on the LOW rail, so the map is not odd about the band. Proven positively: at index 0 both channels agree on the shared low start rather than negating (r[0]=l[0]=L, not r[0]=−l[0]=M).
think Mirrored ALES92's two forms: stereo_schmitt (from silence, per channel) and StereoSchmitt (two SchmittTriggers built with one shared band via a single init so left/right can never drift). The carried-state crux carries into stereo: a two-piece StereoSchmitt run (each channel's second piece continuing THAT channel's ending rail) equals the whole run once byte for byte on both channels — no seam flip on either speaker, ALES92's own crux (the ALES91 shape, one bit per channel) made stereo. Both forms validate the shared band and length ONCE via ALES92's precheck before either channel is touched, so a refusal never triggers one channel or advances one rail — atomicity across two independent bits. SchmittError reused whole.
think Proved all four laws: the stereo schmitt law against ALES92's own mono schmitt run per channel; the balance/length law at even and odd length; the independent-rail law (identical stays identical, out-of-phase not held out of phase, the two rails flip independently — left flips high where right holds low, the zero-width band the plain comparator on both); and the carried-state/atomicity/degenerate law (two-piece = whole on both, inverted band / low-under-floor / high-over-ceiling / bad-span each atomic with both rails untouched, count 0 the identity). Caught and removed one fragile self-test line where the odd relation coincidentally held at index 1 (−l[1]=−M=L=r[1]); the clean parting proof lives at the shared low start (index 0).
obs No custody gate reached — purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, one bit of rail state per channel, a self-approved design round. This rung opens a NEW corner of the stereo NONLINEAR class: the state-carrying comparator beside the memoryless clips. The honest lesson: a memoryless odd map holds the inter-channel antisymmetry under a shared parameter; a comparator that remembers a shared low start does not — each channel remembers its own crossing history, so identical stays identical while phase is per-channel memory, not a preserved symmetry. Witness GREEN (all four laws), tame_style_check bans clean. The next Lotus lap could carry ALES93's zero_cross (the read-only counter that reads schmitt's rail flips) into stereo, or open another mono primitive — a fresh heading rather than a mechanical continuation.
loom witness=ales_stereo_schmitt_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=nonlinear-comparator state=carried rails=independent antisymmetry=parted-from-memoryless crux=carried-state-split-equals-whole cases=stereo-law+balance+identical+parting+rail-independence+zero-width-comparator+two-piece-whole+from-silence-equiv+reset+span+atomicity(inverted,floor,ceiling,range)+degenerate
file lotus/stereo_schmitt.rye ALES144 — stereo_schmitt, the Schmitt trigger lifted to stereo: one shared band, two independent rails, both from-silence stereo_schmitt and carried StereoSchmitt (mirroring ALES92's two forms), four laws with the independent-rail law (identical stays identical, out-of-phase NOT held out of phase — the honest parting from the memoryless odd family) and the carried-state crux (a two-piece run equals the whole once byte for byte on both); runs ALES92's proven mono schmitt per channel, SchmittError and precheck reused whole.
file tools/ales_stereo_schmitt_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-schmitt line.
